{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T05:48:56.584Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d97cc75851de74b9275ff63","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-30tjoh","lineage:pm-30tjoh","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-30tjoh","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-30tjoh","lineage:pm-30tjoh","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"tests/unit/core/item/malformed-annotation-entries.spec.ts seeds a string, a number and a text-less object into comments, notes and learnings. pm <collection> and pm get --json exit 0 through the built CLI, an append keeps all entries, and a guarded edit of a null entry refuses with annotation_entry_mismatch. The comparator spec fails with the item-format.ts fix stashed. The 557 annotation and item specs pass, and every added line is covered."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A malformed annotation entry never produces an unhandled TypeError: reads, appends and guarded edits complete or refuse with a typed error, and the read surfaces agree"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/claim_principal"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T05:48:56.584Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-11-08T05:48:56.565Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-11-08T05:48:56.565Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"compareLogValues, the store's canonical annotation order in src/core/item/item-format.ts, now reads created_at, text and author defensively (logSortFields). A stored entry that is not an object, or lacks a field, sorts by empty strings instead of throwing, so pm comments, pm notes, pm learnings and pm get read such a document. Malformed entries are delivered as stored (PR 1685 stopped spreading them into indexed characters), appends still work and keep them, and the --expect-at guard reads a null entry safely: it refuses with annotation_entry_mismatch, reporting actual_created_at null and an unrecorded-time message, instead of throwing a TypeError. Tolerating rather than refusing keeps a whole item readable when one entry is damaged."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Fixed: malformed comments, notes and learnings entries no longer crash reads"}],"before_hash":"02e869288b3edc4fb119e7f637097da91dacd8680e12cef048ecd2266303a92d","after_hash":"fbc47c87c7c7390a3e09c1358a66ef0b716b09146997bd6a9ad9f3f76b0cc47e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-08T05:48:56.565Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4786f691a276d8586f6d86b316f85c3c3be0661b9258989ce6899c65e292ba57"}
