{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T08:54:00.138Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d97cc75851de74b9275ff63","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-0jzl5t","lineage:pm-0jzl5t","lineage:pm-wzmbvn","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-0jzl5t","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-0jzl5t","lineage:pm-0jzl5t","lineage:pm-wzmbvn","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-08T08:54:00.137Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 4 of PR 1687 (P2, fixed): the canonical annotation order is hashed into item history (canonicalDocument feeds history hashing and replay for every existing hash epoch). The grouping added for the CodeRabbit cycle finding reordered documents the legacy comparator could already sort, for example an ISO stamp next to \"zzzz\". An unchanged stream written before the change then reported verify_failed:after_hash_mismatch:entry_1. The first cut of this fix carried the same risk in a quieter form: it coerced a missing field to \"\", where the legacy localeCompare argument had read \"undefined\". Two entries sharing created_at, one without text, could therefore flip.\n\nThe comparator is now legacy-exact. logSortFields coerces with String(), as the legacy Date.parse and localeCompare arguments were, and the grouping is reverted. Every document the legacy comparator could sort keeps its order and hashes, and null or primitive entries sort instead of throwing. A pairwise spec compares against an inline copy of the legacy comparator wherever that copy does not throw. It fails against both the grouping comparator and the empty-string version. The transitive order for mixed stamps needs a versioned canonicalization transition, filed as pm-yo46im.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T08:54:00.138Z"}],"before_hash":"78f654d6bf485f215d3359efb4fbaa27e633d057f428ac24fdfdb8d90b115ecf","after_hash":"aa15cd3a594f1b26ba1b53f5eac96b45fd21facee337b88dc3bd39e18d23f0a0","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"04bdb1dcf567fe6906ffae745048f4514d4ea6d79ebec5591018fe6201cfa614"}
